  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;be the line passing through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> such that its intercepted segment between the co-ordinate axes is bisected at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is the line perpendicular to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> and passing through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the point of intersection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "c4gJL",
      "text": "<math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>23</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>",
